# Part One | Diagrams
N: This is the lab where everything happens, and that fern is Gerald.
%blocks Context Diagram
- Sensor > MCU:moisture
- MCU (STM32) > Pump:on/off, Phone:Wi-Fi
- Pump
- Phone
ada: Here is a block diagram with arrows and labels between boxes.
ben!: Wait, the pump is connected to what?
%layers Layered Architecture
- Application | watering logic
- Services | scheduler, logging
- Drivers | GPIO, ADC, UART
- Hardware | the actual chip
cy~: Layers. I love layers. Investors love layers.
%code Blink the LED
| #define LED_PIN 5
| int main(void) {
|   gpio_init(LED_PIN);   // set as output
|>  while (1) {
|     gpio_toggle(LED_PIN);
|     delay_ms(500);
|   }
| }
ada>: A tiny program that toggles a pin forever.
@zone bench
%timing I2C Start
- SCL: 1111010101010111
- SDA: 1110==========11 addr,R/W
N@ben?: Ben stares at the timing chart and worries.
%states Watering Machine on=Dry
- Idle > Dry:soil dry
- Dry > Watering:pump on
- Watering > Idle:wet enough
cy^: Ship it!
@zone green
@world droop=0>1
%memory Memory Map
- 0x2000_0000 | RAM | 1 | variables
- 0x0800_8000 | App | 2 | code
- 0x0800_0000 | Bootloader | 1 | 32 KB
ada_: Gerald is drooping again.
%bits GPIOB ODR
bits 00100000
names -,-,LED,-,-,-,-,-
hl 5
label PORTB |= (1 << 5);
N: Bit five is set.
%chart Battery Life
- line Always on: 100,70,40,10,0
- line Sleeping: 100,95,90,85,80
xl Mon,Tue,Wed,Thu,Fri
N: Sleeping saves a lot.
%table Buses
- Bus | Wires | Speed
- UART | 2 | slow
- SPI | 4 | fast
- I2C | 2 | medium
ben^: Got it!
%big 40,000\nwatering cycles | per year, give or take
N: That is a lot of water.
